<title>LEBANON: Lebanon budget deficit 3,187 bln Leb pounds in Oct.</title>
<headline>Lebanon budget deficit 3,187 bln Leb pounds in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's budget deficit rose to 3,187 billion Lebanese pounds at the end of October, compared with a planned deficit of 2,428 billion for the full year under the 1996 budget law, according to finance ministry statistics issued on Friday.</p>
<p>Cumulative spending at the end of October were 5,935 billion pounds including debt servicing payments totalling 2,259 billion. Revenues were 2,748 billion.</p>
<p>It issued the following statistics (in billions of Lebanese pounds):</p>
<p>		  Jan  Feb Mar Apr May Jun Jul Aug Sep Oct     Total</p>
<p> Expenditure  424  483 419 536 576 544 565 612 713 1,063   5,935</p>
<p>Of which interest payments</p>
<p>		   95  148  98 167 189 104 207 224 286   741   2,259</p>
<p> Revenues     251  165 396 181 234 372 244 326 292   287   2,748</p>
<p> Deficit	173  318  23 355 342 172 321 286 421   776   3,187</p>
<p>1996 Budget targets are:</p>
<p> Expenditure			 6,450</p>
<p> Of which interest payments    2,600</p>
<p> Revenues			    4,022</p>
<p> Deficit			     2,428</p>
<p>($1 = 1,555.0 Lebanese pounds)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602057 353078 645456</p>
